{"text": "From: Renczkowski, Daniel (DPH)\n\nSent: Friday, October 06, 2006 9:25 AM\nTo: Khan, Annie (DPH); Salemi, Charles (DPH); Saunders, Della (DPH); O'Brien, Elisabeth\n(DPH); Corbett, Kate (DPH); Tran, Mai (DPH); Medina, Nicole (DPH)\nSubject: FW: Dateline DEA - October 6, 2006\n\nCheck out this link if nothing else:\n\nSent: Friday, October 06, 2006 8:46 AM\nTo: dateline dea@wdecserver01.usdoj.gov\nSubject: Dateline DEA - October 6, 2006\n\nDEA's Biweekly E-mail Informant\n\nOctober 6, 2006\n\nLeaders of the Infamous Cali Cartel Plead Guilty\n\nMiguel and Gilberto Rodriguez-Orejuela, brothers who ran the powerful Cali Cartel in Colombia that was\nresponsible for importing tons of cocaine into the United States over the last two decades, have pleaded guilty\nto a charge of conspiracy to import cocaine into the United States. \"The Rodriguez-Orejuela brothers defined\nthe label \"kingpin,\" said Administrator Karen P. Tandy. \"During little more than a decade, their Cali cartel\nsold at least 30,000 kilos of cocaine and amassed an illicit fortune worth in excess of $1 billion.\"\n\nClick here for the Press Release\n\nClick here for more about the history of the Cali Cartel\n\nSearch Warrants Served at San Francisco Marijuana Distribution Center\n\nDEA made 15 arrests and seized a sophisticated indoor marijuana grow and thousands of marijuana plants. As\npart of the investigation against Remedies Cooperative LLC, (formerly known as Compassionate Caregivers)\nand Potent Employment Solutions, agents also seized 2 vehicles, including a Porsche Carrera convertible, and a\ntotal of $125,000 in U.S. Currency . \"Federal drug laws prohibit the cultivation and sale of marijuana. Anyone\n\n1\n\nCorbett_email_PRR_025493",
